an be weaponized to solve a  problem or even to discover new  opportunities  again we can practice and develop our  creativity but this is also a product of  being able to remain calm  to approach problems with an open mind  to think outside the box and overcome  cognitive biases and to draw from a  large well of information and former  knowledge  using these traits in isolation is not  enough though we must be able to  dynamically shift between them and apply  them in countless combinations  if you can excel in the areas i've  listed here you will be extremely  adaptable to a wide variety of  unpredictable scenarios  this is what georges hebert describes as  being strong to be helpful  this is being ready for anything and  this is what i believe it means to be  truly fit  [Music]  so there you go guys i hope that video  was useful and interesting this is  actually a deviation from my planned  content schedule this month because i  had a  flood in my house and i'm currently  staying at the in-laws with minimal  equipment so hopefully i can get this  video out on time  if it's a week late then i can only  apologize i just think it's useful to  sometimes think about  why you're fit and what the purpose of  all these different traits we're  developing  actually might be i hope it starts a  discussion and i hope you guys found it  interesting  if you guys agree with these ideas and  you want to train in a way that's  actually useful and  could benefit you in a crisis then why  not check out my ebook and training  program  super functional training where i go  into this stuff in much more detail  an outline at the end a program that  will develop not only your strength and  speed but your mobility  your brain power and a whole lot more  alternatively you could check out my  physical book which was recently  published functional training  and beyond that's available from all  good bookstores and it contains a  large discussion around the philosophy  of functional training